/P 193 0 R
/T (Challenges & Lesson learned)
/E (Challenges & Lesson learned)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (The first cohort of Campus Connect was as much a lesson in resilience as it was a milestone for grassroots BCH adoption. Rolling out a program meant to bring Bitcoin Cash education directly to university students came with real friction the kind that doesn't always make it into recap threads, but shaped every step of the journey.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 193 0 R
/T (Travel Bottlenecks)
/E (Travel Bottlenecks)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Coordinating across campuses, sometimes in different states or regions, meant organizers and facilitators had to absorb transport costs and long commute hours just to show up. Poor road networks, unpredictable transport fares, and tight schedules made it difficult to guarantee consistent presence at every campus on the calendar. More than once, sessions had to be rescheduled or condensed because a facilitator was still in transit.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 193 0 R
/T (Low Community Visibility)
/E (Low Community Visibility)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Coordinating across campuses, sometimes in different states or regions, meant organizers and facilitators had to absorb transport costs and long commute hours just to show up. Poor road networks, unpredictable transport fares, and tight schedules made it difficult to guarantee consistent presence at every campus on the calendar. More than once, sessions had to be rescheduled or condensed because a facilitator was still in transit.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 193 0 R
/T (Funding Constraints)
/E (Funding Constraints)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Like most grassroots efforts, funding lagged behind ambition. Stipends for volunteers, printing of educational materials, and even basic session logistics were often self-funded or covered through informal contributions. This limited how many campuses could be reached in the pilot phase and forced organizers to prioritize ruthlessly.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 193 0 R
/T (Space Rental Challenges)
/E (Space Rental Challenges)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Securing suitable venues was harder than expected. Many campuses required formal bookings with fees attached, and last-minute availability issues sometimes forced sessions into cramped or less-than-ideal spaces hardly the environment needed to properly introduce peer-to-peer electronic cash to newcomers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
